{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_011Ch3neXtDT8H36TmtwTjCn","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed `wholsale` to `wholesale` in `data/2025-10.csv`, `data/2025-11.csv` and `data/2025-12.csv`. All three are in one commit, `07b4231`, so a single `git revert 07b4231` undoes it. `scripts/check.sh` printed `OK` before the commit, though it only checks field counts. A final grep finds no `wholsale` left anywhere in the repo.\n\n- **Commit prefix:** the message starts with `2025-12`, the latest month touched, since `CLAUDE.md` wants a month prefix and the commit spans three.\n- **`inbox/2025-12.csv`:** it had the same typo and I fixed it too, but git doesn't track it, so it isn't in the commit. The earlier `git ls-files inbox` output was misleading and the file doesn't appear in the repo. `git status` stays clean, which suggests the inbox is ignored or excluded.\n- **A slip along the way:** my first commit attempt failed because I hadn't staged the files. Nothing was committed then, and the second attempt succeeded.\n- **`data/2026-01.csv`:** I left it alone as you asked, so line 33 is still malformed.","citations":[]}],"model":"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":396,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":349,"cache_read_input_tokens":19415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":349,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":"standard","speed":"standard"},"provider":"Anthropic","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<uuid-1>","uuid":"<uuid-60>","timestamp":"2026-11-15T00:44:11.914Z","request_id":"gen-1794703447-RXxbrlPqFewDwSfzZm9n"}
